    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "20 Best Bangkok Hotels, From Grande Dames to Converted Canal Homes",
        "main_title": "20 Best Bangkok Hotels, From Grande Dames to Converted Canal Homes",
        "author": "Jenny Adams",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "When it comes to value-for-your-money hotels, this is one of the best cities in the world.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Some things in Bangkok will hopefully never change. May there always be noodles, curries, and spicy soups to enjoy, whether it’s sit-down fine dining or a well-loved curbside wok. May the Chao Phraya river, lined by palm trees and longtail boats, continue to burble and buoy commerce, and the skyline, with its wild dichotomy of futuristic glassy skyscrapers and ancient golden-tile temples, continue to light up the area.",
            "url": "https://www.cntraveler.com/story/the-chefs-designers-and-activists-transforming-bangkok",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.cntraveler.com/story/the-chefs-designers-and-activists-transforming-bangkok",
                "anchor_text": "Bangkok"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.cntraveler.com/gallery/best-restaurants-in-bangkok",
                "anchor_text": "dining"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The details of the city, however, never fail to surprise me on every return visit. So much is consistently new, and it’s never more evident than in the hotel game. The globe’s best brands are here (welcoming the millions who visit annually is serious business), providing inventive experiences, over-the-top amenities, Michelin-worthy food, and spas, spas, spas.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2025 alone, Aman returned with something new and innovative (the brand, which began in Thailand 18 years ago, opened the Aman Nai Lert, on the edge of the hyper-trendy Phloen Chit neighborhood), and the Mandarin Oriental debuted a fresh restaurant under a two-star Michelin chef. For something smaller, The Siamotif—a cute, century-old canal bungalow—is an art lover’s top choice, and the Bangkok Publishing Residence features eight rooms and a literary history. Simply put, Bangkok is one of the best cities in the world for those who adore hotels, full of luxury resorts, rustic respites, homestay-style boutiques, and more. Read on for our list of the best hotels in Bangkok in 2025.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "In this article:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
